Body:
> Possibly related: in Nanocoder the fix was to disable some timeouts: [Nano-Collective/nanocoder#441 (comment)](https://github.com/Nano-Collective/nanocoder/issues/441#issuecomment-4224415299) . OpenCode might have similar configurable options.

I am experiencing a very similar issue.  I've tried the suggested workaround, but that did not fix it for me.  Here's my config:
```
{
  "$schema": "https://opencode.ai/config.json",
  "tools": {
      "task": false,
      "webfetch": false,
      "todowrite": false
  },
  "model": "ollama/qwen3.5-32k-nothink",
  "small_model": "ollama/qwen3.5-32k-nothink",
  "provider": {
    "ollama": {
      "npm": "@ai-sdk/openai-compatible",
      "options": {
          "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1",
	  "requestTimeout": -1,
	  "socketTimeout": -1,
          "apiKey": "ollama"
      },
      "models": {
        "qwen3.5-32k-nothink": {
          "tools": true
        }
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Also I noticed that while looking at the Opencode - ollama communication by redirecting the url to a 8080 proxy via `mitmdump` I see that the responce message gets dumped only after the Opencode prompt is cancelled (by pressing Escape twice after sending a simple prompt).
